  - Assumption satisfaction: Random Forest and XGBoost do not require strict assumptions.
  - Failure modes: Logistic Regression may underperform if relationships are non-linear.

Selected Method: Random Forest, justified by its robustness and ability to handle complex relationships.

Quality validation: Cross-validate to ensure model generalization.

### Decision 3: Validation Strategy
Candidate Methods:
  A) **K-Fold Cross-Validation**: Standard method for model validation.
     - Pros: Reduces variance in performance estimates.
     - Cons: Computationally expensive.
  
  B) **Stratified K-Fold**: Ensures class distribution is maintained.
     - Pros: Better for imbalanced datasets.
     - Cons: Slightly more complex.
  
  C) **Leave-One-Out Cross-Validation**: Each sample is used for validation once.
     - Pros: Utilizes all data.
     - Cons: Very computationally expensive.

Selected Method: Stratified K-Fold Cross-Validation, justified by the class imbalance in the TARGET variable.
