
EVALUATION METRIC: Weighted categorization accuracy, calculated as:
$$\text{weighted_accuracy}(y, \hat{y}) = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^{n} \frac{w_i  (y_i = \hat{y}_i)}{\sum{w_i}} $$
where $w_i$ is 0.7 for unaltered images and 0.3 for altered images.

CONSTRAINTS: 
- Memory: Must handle large image datasets efficiently.
- Time: Must complete within the competition deadlines.
- Data distribution: Must account for altered and unaltered images.

ASSUMPTIONS: 
- The intrinsic features of images from different camera models are distinguishable.
- The alterations applied to images do not completely obscure the camera model's signature.

KNOWN FAILURE MODES:
  - Risk 1: Class imbalance between altered and unaltered images.
  - Risk 2: Overfitting to the training data due to limited samples per camera model.

SUCCESS CRITERIA: 
- Achieve a weighted accuracy above a predefined threshold on the validation set.
- Generate a valid submission file that meets the competition requirements.
</reasoning>
